Color Shades — standalone native Rust extension for Tezbar

Original extension: Color Shades by qeude, Raycast extensions commit
6734d85992290066fd31a7f5bee3cca3d3545a1a, extensions/color-shades, MIT
(licenses/raycast-extensions-MIT.txt). The original TypeScript source, command
names, arguments and icon are preserved in this repository. Own V1/V2/process
adaptation copyright 2026 almatkai, MIT (LICENSE, licenses/color-shades-port-MIT.txt).

Bundled data and ported algorithms (compiled into bin/tezbar-color-shades):
- Name that Color dataset by Chirag Mehta, CC-BY-2.5
  (licenses/name-that-color-CC-BY-2.5.txt; source http://chir.ag/projects/ntc/).
  All 1,566 names, values and order are unchanged; camelCase export slugs were
  generated with change-case-all 1.0.15 (and camel-case, pascal-case, no-case; MIT).
- color-namer 1.4.0 by Zeke Sikelianos, MIT (licenses/color-namer-MIT.md).
- chroma-js 1.4.1 by Gregor Aisch, BSD-3-Clause (licenses/chroma-js-BSD-3-Clause.txt):
  Lab distance constants and operation order are ported.
- color-convert 2.0.1 by Heather Arthur, MIT (licenses/color-convert-MIT.txt).

Runtime Rust crates: tezbar-extension-sdk 0.1.1 at immutable git revision
aaec571673ab64a85a136cf6bd054ef660c4d93c, Apache-2.0
(licenses/tezbar-extension-sdk-Apache-2.0.txt; Copyright 2026 Almat). Other crates
and their SPDX expressions are listed in licenses/rust-dependencies.txt. Original
crate license and notice texts, including Unicode-3.0 for unicode-ident, are
preserved under licenses/rust/<crate>-<version>/.

No JavaScript, npm package, network lookup or Raycast API is used at runtime.
Combined SPDX expression:
MIT AND Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause AND CC-BY-2.5 AND Unicode-3.0.
